# IWFCam RTSP bridge

The service starts automatically at boot, but waits until the configured
camera MAC address is visible on the local Wi-Fi station or neighbor table.
It does not require Internet access or cloud discovery.

Configuration is in `/etc/config/iwfcam`:

```sh
uci set iwfcam.main.camera_ip='10.41.0.101'
uci set iwfcam.main.camera_mac='c6:26:08:13:2e:23'
uci commit iwfcam
/etc/init.d/iwfcam restart
```

The default stream is:

```text
rtsp://<node-ip>:8554/cam
```

RTSP over TCP/interleaved transport is recommended for lossy long-range
HaLow links. The bridge carries the camera's H.264 stream without requiring
the camera to reach the Internet.
